{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-77-1","title":"Psalms 77:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The psalmist shews what fierce combat he had with diffidence. 10 The victory which he had by consideration of God's great and gracious works.</p>\n<p>A.M. cir. 3463. B.C. cir. 541. (Title.) Jeduthun. 39:1; 62:1; *titles 1Ch 16:41,42; 25:3,6 A Psalm.This Psalm is allowed by the best judges to have been written during the Babylonian captivity.</p>\n<p>of Asaph. or, for Asaph. 50:1; *title I cried. 3:4; 34:6; 55:16,17; 142:1-3 gave. 116:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-2","title":"Psalms 77:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>In the. 18:6; 50:15; 88:1-3; 102:1,2; 130:1,2; Ge 32:7-12,28 2Ki 19:3,4,15-20; Isa 26:9,16; Jon 2:1,2; 2Co 12:7,8; Heb 5:7 my. 6:2,3; 38:3-8; 2Ch 6:28; Isa 1:5,6; Ho 5:13; 6:1 sore. Heb. hand. my soul. Ge 37:35; Es 4:1-4; Pr 18:14; Jer 31:15; Joh 11:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-3","title":"Psalms 77:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I remembered. Job 6:4; 23:15,16; 31:23; Jer 17:17 I complained. 88:3-18; 102:3-28; Job 7:11; La 3:17,39 spirit. 55:4,5; 61:2; 142:2,3; 143:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-4","title":"Psalms 77:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>holdest. 6:6; Es 6:1; Job 7:13-15 I am. Job 2:13; 6:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-5","title":"Psalms 77:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>74:12-18; 143:5; De 32:7; Isa 51:9; 63:9-15; Mic 7:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-6","title":"Psalms 77:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>my song. 42:8; Job 35:10; Hab 3:17,18; Jon 1:2; Ac 16:25 commune. 4:4; Ec 1:16 and. 139:23,24; Job 10:2; La 3:40; 1Co 11:28-32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-7","title":"Psalms 77:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>the Lord. 13:1,2; 37:24; 74:1; 89:38,46; Jer 23:24-26; La 3:31,32; Ro 11:1,2 and will. 79:5; 85:1,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-8","title":"Psalms 77:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Is his. Isa 27:11; Lu 16:25,26 doth. Nu 14:34; 23:19; Jer 15:18; Ro 9:6 for evermore. Heb. to generation and generation.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-9","title":"Psalms 77:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>God. Isa 40:27; 49:14,15; 63:15 shut up. Lu 13:25-28; Ro 11:32; *marg: 1Jo 3:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-10","title":"Psalms 77:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>This is, etc.Or, as Dr. Waterland renders, \"This my affliction is a change of the right hand of the Most High,\" i.e., it proceeds from a change of God's conduct towards me. De Dieu renders, {Precari, hoc meum est; mutare dextram Altissimi:} \"To pray, this is my business: to change the right hand of the Most High.\" I can do nothing else than pray: God is the Ruler of events. Mr. N. M. Berlin translates, {Dolere meum hoc est: mutare est dextr� Altissimi:} \"To grieve is my portion: to change (my condition) belongs to the right hand of the Most High.\"</p>\n<p>31:22; 73:22; 116:11; Job 42:3; La 3:18-23; Mr 9:24 the years. 5; Ex 15:6; Nu 23:21,22; De 4:34; Hab 3:2-13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-11","title":"Psalms 77:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>10; 28:5; 78:11; 111:4; 1Ch 16:12; Isa 5:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-12","title":"Psalms 77:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>meditate. 104:34; 143:5 talk. 71:24; 105:2; 145:4,11; De 6:7; Lu 24:14-32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-13","title":"Psalms 77:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Thy way. 27:4; 63:2; 68:25; 73:17 who. 89:6-8; Ex 15:11; De 32:31; Isa 40:18,25; 46:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-14","title":"Psalms 77:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>the God. 72:18; 86:10; 105:5; 136:4; Ex 15:11; Re 15:3 thou hast. Ex 13:14; 15:6; Jos 9:9,10; Isa 51:9; 52:10; Da 3:29; 6:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-15","title":"Psalms 77:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>with. 136:11,12; Ex 6:6; De 9:26,29; Isa 63:9 the sons. Ge 48:3-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-16","title":"Psalms 77:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>114:3-6; Ex 14:21; Jos 3:15,16; Hab 3:8-10,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-17","title":"Psalms 77:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>poured out like water. Heb. were poured forth with water. 68:8,9 thine. 18:14; 144:6; 2Sa 22:15; Hab 3:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-18","title":"Psalms 77:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>voice. 29:3-9; Ex 19:16; Job 37:1-5; Re 11:19 lightnings. 97:4; Hab 3:4; Re 18:1 earth. Ex 19:18; 2Sa 22:8,14; Mt 27:51; 28:2; Re 20:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-19","title":"Psalms 77:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>way. 29:10; 97:2; Ne 9:11; Na 1:3,4; Hab 3:15 footsteps. Ex 14:28; Ro 11:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-77-20","title":"Psalms 77:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":77,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":77,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>78:52; 80:1; Ex 13:21; 14:19; Isa 63:11,12; Ho 12:13; Ac 7:35,36</p>"}]}